## Phase 4: Iteration & Measurement (Ongoing)

### Step 4a: Create test cases

```
TEST_CASE_1: Publication from new source
Input: 24-page academic paper
Expected: Title 50–80 chars, summary 150–180 words, 2–4 themes

TEST_CASE_2: Edge case
Input: Cross-cutting topic (not hazard-specific)
Expected: Hazard tag OMITTED, themes from vocabulary
```

### Step 4b: Measure success

| Metric | Target | How |
|--------|--------|-----|
| First-attempt accuracy | 80%+ | % of AI outputs passing review without revision |
| Time savings | 50%+ | Before vs. after editor time per article |
| Consistency | 95%+ | % of metadata matching vocabulary |

Track in spreadsheet:
```
Date | Content | Matches Guidance? | Editor Changes | Time Saved
2026-01-15 | Publication 1 | Yes | None | 20 min
2026-01-15 | Publication 2 | Partial | 2 corrections | 10 min
```

### Step 4c: Quarterly audits

Every 3 months:
1. Export last 25 published items (new content)
2. Measure against guidance (accuracy %)
3. Collect editor feedback
4. Update AGENT_GUIDANCE.md with refinements
5. Log changes in DECISIONS.md

**Example DECISIONS.md entry:**
```
2026-04-01 | Expanded theme limit from 3–4 to 2–5
Reason: Found 5 high-performing articles with 5 themes
Change: Updated AGENT_GUIDANCE.md
Source: Quarterly audit (March 2026)
```

